958,50,115,26]],"links":[["Sheridan County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/montana/sheridan-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sheridan County","/arc-plc/montana/sheridan-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 14 grids came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years for October to November, the most of any pair since 1951. In 2026 so far, April to May came in at 33% of normal on the middle of the grids, and January to February at 64%. June to July is the wettest pair at 4.99 inches of normal, and January to February is the driest at 0.70. Grid 34303 had its driest year in 2017 at 52% of normal.</p>"}
